From: ASUS Zenbook A14 Linux support
Subject: [PATCH] power-profiles: present the five current A14 modes

The A14 bridge uses standard PPD wire names where possible while the hardware
policy is Whisper / Quiet / Normal / Turbo / Full Speed. GNOME Shell 50 filters
profiles through PROFILE_PARAMS and labels the standard three with generic
names, so teach the existing Power Mode tile both A14-specific names and the
A14 presentation labels. All five presentation icons use the same A14 symbolic
API names, backed by the ordered Yaru meter family.

Internal PPD name -> A14 UI name:
  power-saver -> Whisper
  quiet       -> Quiet
  balanced    -> Normal
  performance -> Turbo
  full-speed  -> Full Speed

--- a/js/ui/status/powerProfiles.js
+++ b/js/ui/status/powerProfiles.js
@@ -14,21 +14,32 @@ const PowerProfilesProxy = Gio.DBusProxy.makeProxyWrapper(PowerProfilesIface);
 
 const PROFILE_PARAMS = {
+    'full-speed': {
+        name: C_('Power profile', 'Full Speed'),
+        iconName: 'a14-power-profile-full-speed-symbolic',
+    },
+
     'performance': {
-        name: C_('Power profile', 'Performance'),
-        iconName: 'power-profile-performance-symbolic',
+        name: C_('Power profile', 'Turbo'),
+        iconName: 'a14-power-profile-turbo-symbolic',
     },
 
     'balanced': {
-        name: C_('Power profile', 'Balanced'),
-        iconName: 'power-profile-balanced-symbolic',
+        name: C_('Power profile', 'Normal'),
+        iconName: 'a14-power-profile-normal-symbolic',
     },
 
     'power-saver': {
-        name: C_('Power profile', 'Power Saver'),
-        iconName: 'power-profile-power-saver-symbolic',
+        name: C_('Power profile', 'Whisper'),
+        iconName: 'a14-power-profile-whisper-symbolic',
     },
+
+    'quiet': {
+        name: C_('Power profile', 'Quiet'),
+        iconName: 'a14-power-profile-quiet-symbolic',
+    },
 };
